      "Prototype the interaction at the fidelity the question needs: low fidelity for sequence, high fidelity for timing and feedback.",
      "Evaluate with users and other evidence: usability tests, think-aloud sessions and expert review. Output: problems ranked by impact.",
      "Refine and test again; iteration continues until the evidence says the interaction works for its users.",
      "Specify the behaviour for implementation: states, transitions, timing, feedback, errors, focus and accessibility. Output: an interaction specification.",
      "Evaluate the real implementation: built systems differ from prototypes in timing, data and edge cases, so check the live behaviour.",
