  evidence: "professional-guideline",
  evidenceNote:
    "Interaction design is a discipline, not a single finding. Its guidance rests on several kinds of evidence: robust experimental regularities for some claims (pointing time, skilled performance models), influential theoretical analyses (direct manipulation, the action cycle, situated action), studies of design and evaluation methods, and a large body of consolidated professional judgement in textbooks, practitioner methods and standards. The two textbooks cited for its scope are recorded bibliographically and are used for what the discipline covers, not as proof of specific effects. Treat principles and patterns as reasons to design and test, not as guarantees.",

